=== QA v5 session 011 — SCALE AUDIT (Audit B) ===
Date: 2026-09-26

--- B.1 Real-range scale test execution ---
$ cargo test test_sim_input_scales_real_abs_range_to_logical -- --nocapture
test_sim_input_scales_real_abs_range_to_logical: skipped (no touch event delivered by libinput — timing/device issue)
test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 40 filtered out

Reran 3x — SKIPPED 100% of runs ("no touch event delivered by libinput").
Also ran under sudo (root) — SKIPPED with the same message.

VERDICT B.1: VACUOUS IN EXECUTION. The test is non-vacuous in DESIGN
  (injects raw 16383/63 with abs_max=32767/127, would assert x≈1085, y≈30),
  but the libinput dispatch/delivery path fails to surface a Touch event
  within the 50ms sleep window, so the test hits the `let Some(contacts)
  else { return; }` skip branch (sim_input.rs:330-336) and marks itself
  "ok" WITHOUT ever asserting the transform. This is the EXACT
  vacuous-pass hazard flagged in Claim 1's CRITICAL note: the test's
  input ranges (32767/127) ≠ output ranges (2170/60) by construction,
  but the assertion never runs, so the real transform is UNVERIFIED by
  execution on this bench.

--- B.2 Stray 2170/60/32767/127 constants outside geometry.rs + test fixtures ---
$ grep -rn "2170\|SIM_WIDTH\|SIM_HEIGHT" src/

PRODUCTION stray constants (NOT in geometry.rs, NOT in test fixtures):
  src/main.rs:55       const ESC_THRESHOLD: u16 = 2170;       [auto-ESC width gate]
  src/main.rs:198      .unwrap_or((60, 2170));                 [tb_dims fallback if display_info fails]
  src/widgets/slider.rs:92   delta_x / 2170.0                  [slider swipe scale — hardcoded bar width]
  src/providers/sim_display.rs:98  const SIM_H: u16 = 2170;    [sim framebuffer height]
  src/providers/sim_input.rs:43   const SIM_WIDTH: i32 = 2170; [sim ABS_MT default + SCALE DENOMINATOR in poll]
  src/providers/sim_input.rs:44   const SIM_HEIGHT: i32 = 60;  [sim ABS_MT default + SCALE DENOMINATOR in poll]
  src/providers/sim_input.rs:223,224,231,232  x_transformed(SIM_WIDTH as u32) / y_transformed(SIM_HEIGHT as u32)
                                                       [poll() scale denominators — HARDCODED, not Geometry]

VERDICT B.2: PARTIAL WIRING. ADR-024 claim "denominators wired to Geometry
  (no duplicated 2170/60/32767/127 constants outside geometry.rs + test
  fixtures)" is REFUTED for the sim provider:
  - input.rs (REAL provider): poll() uses self.tb_dims (Geometry-derived) ✓
  - sim_input.rs (SIM provider): poll() uses hardcoded SIM_WIDTH/SIM_HEIGHT (2170/60) ✗
  The sim scale denominators are NOT derived from Geometry. They happen to
  match the real logical dims (2170/60), so the real-range test WOULD
  exercise a real 32767→2170 / 127→60 scale IF it ran — but the
  denominators are constants, not Geometry-derived. A future panel with
  different dims would need a sim_input.rs code edit.
  Other strays (ESC_THRESHOLD, slider 2170, fallback) are pre-existing
  and out of ADR-024's stated scope (the ADR scoped only the input
  provider scale target), but they remain duplicated 2170 constants.

